# `slice.call(arguments, 1)` in a copy: the state holds every element of the object, so the slice is a list of them, which the reads behind it are answered out of. Nothing is made and no built-in is called.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: CallBuiltin
# CHECK-NOT: CreateUnmappedArguments
# CHECK-NOT: CreateMappedArguments
# CHECK-NOT: NewArray
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f2 mechanisms=-EscapeAnalysis
# WITHHELD: CallBuiltin {{*}}ArrayPrototypeSlice
